              "text": "やかん (yakan) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are yaku, \"medicine\" (Middle Chinese yak) and kan, \"jar\" (kwanH, the reading of its fuller older form) (Unihan, KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription). It was a pot for brewing medicine, and yaku shortened to ya; JMdict marks it as usually written in kana."
